    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0262",
      "sequence": 274,
      "meaning": "The Lord casts the two pieces of the bow upon the ground, and everyone becomes joyful. The sage Kauśika’s body seems a purifying ocean beautifully plunged into the water of love; beholding the full moon of Rāma’s form, great waves of rapture rise. Celestial drums thunder in the sky; heavenly women dance and sing. Brahmā and the other gods, siddhas and great sages praise the Lord and give blessings, showering flowers and many-coloured garlands while Kinnaras sing sweet songs. Cries of victory fill the worlds, and the bow’s breaking roar seems endless. Everywhere men and women exult that Rāma has broken Śiva’s mighty bow. Heralds, Māgadhas and bardic charioteers recite praises with steady understanding, while people offer up horses, elephants, wealth, jewels and garments.",
