    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0264",
      "sequence": 276,
      "meaning": "How does Sītā shine among her friends? Like supreme Beauty among assembled forms of beauty. The victory garland glows in her lotus hand, covered by the splendour of victory over the world. Her body is modest while her mind brims with highest delight; no one can discern her hidden love. Drawing near and beholding Rāma’s beauty, the princess stands like a painted figure. Perceiving this, her clever friends prompt her to place the lovely victory garland upon him. Hearing them, she raises the garland in both hands but, overwhelmed by love, cannot put it on. With her stalk-like paired arms, she seems a pair of lotuses fearfully offering a victory garland to the moon. Her companions sing as they behold the scene, and Sītā sets the garland upon Rāma’s breast. Seeing it there, the gods shower flowers; all the rulers shrink like night-lilies before the sun.",
